{"name":"Confectionary","hex":"#d4b4d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"confectionary","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to, or of the nature of confections or their production.","Prepared as a confection."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A candy, sweetmeat; a confection.","A place where confections are manufactured, stored; a confectory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confectionary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Confectionery","blocks":[{"text":"Confectionery is the art of making confections, or sweet foods. Confections are items that are rich in sugar and carbohydrates, although exact definitions are difficult. In general, however, confections are divided into two broad and somewhat overlapping categories: baker's confections and sugar confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Krokan.jpg/330px-Krokan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confectionery","wikidata":"Q5159627"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Yasnaya_Polyana_Confectionery_Factory_01.jpg/500px-Yasnaya_Polyana_Confectionery_Factory_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Yasnaya_Polyana_Confectionery_Factory_01.jpg/500px-Yasnaya_Polyana_Confectionery_Factory_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Confectionery can be mass-produced in a factory.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYasnaya_Polyana_Confectionery_Factory_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Chum_chums.jpg/500px-Chum_chums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Chum_chums.jpg/500px-Chum_chums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org